WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.059
- Hello, everyone, I'm Maurice Samuels,

00:00:07.059 --> 00:00:09.560
the Director of the Yale Program

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.500
for the Study of Antisemitism.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.600
And it's my great pleasure
to welcome you today

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.420
to our Benjamin and Barbara
Zucker Lecture Series.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.740
I'm pretty sure this is our first lecture

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.960
on the topic of Antisemitism
in South America.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.690
The plan for today will be

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.800
that I will introduce the speaker.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.720
He'll talk for about 40 minutes,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.720
and then we'll open it up to questions

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.460
from the audience.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.640
Please submit your questions at any time

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.430
during the lecture, using the Q&amp;A function

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.080
at the bottom of your
screen and I will ask them.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:47.450
The chat function is
disabled, so don't use that.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.380
Today's speaker, Emmanuel Kahan,

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.850
holds a PhD in History and Memory Studies

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:58.110
from the National University
of La Plata, Buenos Aires.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.460
And he's a Researcher

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.800
at the National Council for Scientific

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:06.030
and Technological Research,
CONICET, in Argentina.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.900
He's also a professor in
the history department

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.600
at the National University of La Plata,

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.560
and teaches post graduate courses

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.540
in different higher education institutions

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:18.660
throughout Argentina.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:22.580
He's the academic coordinator
of the Jewish Studies Program

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:25.700
at the Institute for Economic
and Social Development

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.150
in Buenos Aires,

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.130
as well as the education
program for teachers

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:33.710
on the Holocaust and other
20th Century Genocides

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:36.610
within the National Plan
for Teachers' Education

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.120
in Argentina.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.350
He's also an affiliated researcher

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.850
at the Center for
Advanced Genocide Research

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.173
at the Shoah Foundation at USC.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.420
He's the author of
several books in Spanish

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.100
on topics ranging from
the Jewish experience

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.120
during Argentina's military dictatorship

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.480
to the Israel-Palestine
conflict in Argentina,

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.170
as well as one book in English,

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:04.170
Memories that Lie a Little
published by Brill in 2018.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.050
In 2013, he received

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.620
the American Jewish Studies Association's

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.330
Best Dissertation Award.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:15.060
And in 2015, he was awarded
the Scientific Work Prize

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.220
by the National University of La Plata.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.150
The title of his talk today,

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:23.020
is Antisemitism in Argentina,

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.730
Historical Experience, Public Debate

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:27.530
and Changing Meanings.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:29.690
Please join me in welcoming Emmanuel.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:31.220
Thank you.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.330
- Thank you, Maurice Samuels.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:36.110
Thank you, everybody for being here

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.793
and coming for listen to me.

00:02:41.185 --> 00:02:42.020
You know I am from Argentina.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.270
English is not my language,

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:46.060
so I apologize for some
mistakes I'm going to make,

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:46.893
I'm going to do.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:52.239
I'm going to share my screen,

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:54.283
I have some slides to present.

00:02:57.988 --> 00:03:01.010
So, please, I think that now
we are seeing the presentation.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:06.660
Well, some years ago in the
framework of a conference

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.110
on Latin American Jewish studies

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.000
I witnessed a series of debates

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.263
about how to approach the
Jewish experience in our region.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.920
In one of the exchange,

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.750
a researcher working from abroad

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:19.692
on the experience of
Jewish life in Argentina

00:03:19.692 --> 00:03:22.647
(indistinct) quote,

00:03:22.647 --> 00:03:24.770
"Whoever reviews the bibliography

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.460
on the history of
Argentine Jewish community

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.290
could conclude that the
life of Jews in the country,

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.750
since they wake up until
they go back to sleep,

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:33.722
is an ordeal.

00:03:33.722 --> 00:03:37.040
Antisemitism is a widespread practice

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.870
that threatens their existence.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.840
However, those of us

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.110
who know the development
of institutional life

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:48.040
as well as unaffiliated Jews,
we know that is not the case."

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:48.873
End of quote.

00:03:50.146 --> 00:03:52.380
With a bit of grace,
this statement challenged

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.990
one of the perspective
that had been central

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.110
to the development on de-semitization

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:00.000
of fields of Jewish studies itself.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.540
Research on antisemitism in my country

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.100
had revealed a concrete
and significant experience

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.750
of the Jewish life in Argentina,

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:10.680
but in turn, they had
cemented a distorted image

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.310
about integration of Jewish
into political, social,

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.733
economic, and cultural life in my country.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.460
A contemporary look at
antisemitism in my country

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:24.280
could not fail to notice
at least three dimensions.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.300
In the first place,

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.950
it's conditioned as a
modern historical experience

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.440
that even when it is a global phenomenon

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.350
has situated imprints.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:33.562
Second, the reception use

00:04:33.562 --> 00:04:34.395
and circulations of
antisemitism in Argentina

00:04:34.395 --> 00:04:39.395
has particular characteristics.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.930
A long history that mobilize
a wide group of factors

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:45.840
and that materializes
in a series of events

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.400
of criminal scopes.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.570
The Tragic Week in 1919,

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:53.150
the closure of Jewish
schools during the '30s,

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.150
the attacks, prosecutions, and murders

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:58.290
promote by right wing Catholic
nationalities organizations

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.530
in the '50s and '60s,

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:03.850
the special treatment
of the Jewish detains

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:06.000
during the last dictatorship,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.800
and finally, the terrorist attack

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.830
against the Israel,
Israelite Mutual Association

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.223
of Argentina, AMIA in 1994.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.141
Third, the formation as a
consequence of the foregoing

00:05:16.141 --> 00:05:20.620
of a wide and diverse
series of organizations

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.453
that devote themselves at each time

00:05:21.453 --> 00:05:26.433
to denouncing anti-Semitic
speech and practices.

00:05:26.433 --> 00:05:29.630
The cause of this
organizations can be rebelling.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:32.660
At times, strategies for
denouncing antisemitism

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:33.547
were one of the engines of recognition

00:05:33.547 --> 00:05:34.380
in the public space

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:39.380
of the uniqueness of the Jewish
experience in the country.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.520
But at the same time,

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.580
they were able to hold
a speech confronting

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:46.782
the victims of the
persecutions against them.

00:05:46.782 --> 00:05:50.720
This presentation aim to programatize

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.415
these last two dimensions

00:05:52.415 --> 00:05:54.480
through a series of racist preference

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:57.100
based on the existing bibliographic review

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.241
and the survey of document
resulting from my research

00:05:59.241 --> 00:06:01.340
on the Buenos Aires Police
Intelligence reports

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.594
and the consultation of
collections on the experience

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:06.670
of life Jewish

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.523
during the last military dictatorship.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.513
The work of Daniel Ivovich

00:06:12.513 --> 00:06:17.120
investigates the origin of
an anti-Semitic narrative

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.940
since the end of 19th century

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:22.730
among actors ascribed to
Argentine Catholic Nationalism.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:23.678
This study let us know

00:06:23.678 --> 00:06:26.707
the effects that these
early representations

00:06:26.707 --> 00:06:29.160
had on the construction of an enemy

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.610
within the nationalist discourse

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:34.833
that had its heyday between 1932 and 1943.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.680
The appearance of these ideas

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:39.513
and proposals around the Jewish question

00:06:39.513 --> 00:06:42.335
combined process of origin

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:44.740
and consolidation of a
nationalist discourse

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:47.013
of a restrictive and an totalitarian type

00:06:47.013 --> 00:06:50.140
in opposition to the liberal
and iterating discourse

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:53.220
that the ruling classes, the elites,

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.663
had in the last third of the 19th century.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.860
This nationalist discourse
was have strong links

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:01.180
with the Catholic church

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:04.410
and with sectors of the
Argentine Armed Forces

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:06.350
that would link the idea of nationality

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:07.183
to the Catholic religion.

00:07:07.183 --> 00:07:10.570
Catholic, sorry.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:13.772
The reception of the
Dreyfus affair, sorry,

00:07:13.772 --> 00:07:17.200
at the end of 19th century
was a starting point

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.430
around the dissemination
of conspiracy theories

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.380
about Jewish by Argentine (indistinct).

00:07:22.222 --> 00:07:24.250
It will be on the characterization

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.224
of the need of the world Jewish conspiracy

00:07:26.224 --> 00:07:27.057
that the common denominator of

00:07:27.057 --> 00:07:31.890
Argentine restricting
nationalists was consecrated.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:34.670
This theory made it possible to articulate

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:35.503
in the same speech

00:07:35.503 --> 00:07:37.740
the figure of particular enemy,

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.634
the Jews, the attacks
on liberal democracy,

00:07:40.634 --> 00:07:43.110
and the denunciation of communist danger

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:45.163
as well as of English imperialism.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:47.396
Although the effects of this
speech around mass mobilization

00:07:47.396 --> 00:07:52.396
proved limited quote,

00:07:52.887 --> 00:07:54.970
"Their recurring use and the political

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:57.620
and literary works that they inspired,

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.840
their use in the political speeches

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:02.220
and as an electoral weapon,

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:05.027
the fact that they have
circulated in the Forces Armies

00:08:05.027 --> 00:08:08.900
and above all, the violent
practices that it inspired

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:09.733
show that its influenced is
far from being marginal."

00:08:09.733 --> 00:08:13.573
End of quote.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:18.080
These narratives combine
a series of practices

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:21.220
that prove ominous for
Jewish in Argentina.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:23.370
The Tragic Week in 1919

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:25.940
considered the first
program in South America

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.160
left uncertain toll of victims

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:30.530
and the consecration of
the figure of the Russian,

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:33.931
the Jews, as a political agitator.

00:08:33.931 --> 00:08:37.540
The massacre against the Jews
in Balvanera neighborhood

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.610
took place in the
context of the repression

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:42.035
of the Barcelona factory strike.

00:08:42.035 --> 00:08:45.260
The repression on the Jewish
quarter of Buenos Aires

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:46.134
was justify by deeply root
belief amongst the elites

00:08:46.134 --> 00:08:46.967
and petit bourgeois about
the Jewish character

00:08:46.967 --> 00:08:47.800
of the revolution that
were taking place in Europe

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:48.633
and from now on

00:08:48.633 --> 00:08:53.633
the Incipient Union of
Soviet Socialistic Republics.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:05.790
Antisemitism will constitute since then,

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:09.060
and at least until '80s and '90s

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:12.360
one of the ideological supports
of conservative nationalist

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.433
and Catholic sectors in my country.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.657
However, not all
nationalists, conservatives

00:09:19.657 --> 00:09:21.690
and Catholics support antisemitism,

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.652
but as the others who
have dedicate themselves

00:09:24.652 --> 00:09:27.297
to the study of right-wing organizations

00:09:27.297 --> 00:09:30.320
formed narratives of hatred towards Jews

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.930
were found wide expressed

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:35.510
within this universe of
programmatic perspectives.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:36.343
It's weight among the elites

00:09:36.343 --> 00:09:39.530
and the state officials
in various governments

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:40.684
was marking the pools of
a series of provisions

00:09:40.684 --> 00:09:41.517
tending to restrict the activities

00:09:41.517 --> 00:09:46.517
of the various Jewish organization,

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.460
as well as to homogenize the population

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:52.463
in relation to Catholic,
Apostolic, and Roman worship.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:56.350
In this sense, the closure
of the Jewish working class

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:58.010
schools during the '30s

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:00.480
or the introduction of
the compulsory teaching

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:05.480
of Catholic religion with the
military government in 1943

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:08.303
may be illustrative of
how this imprint operated.

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:13.510
At this point, it's necessary to replace

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:14.770
one of the classic debates,

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:17.140
both in the field of
political representations

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:19.150
as well as among historians.

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:23.415
The allegedly Anti-Semitic
character of Peronism.

00:10:23.415 --> 00:10:24.980
It is a controversy that

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.056
as the words of Andrés Bisso point out,

00:10:26.056 --> 00:10:26.889
was contemporary to the
emergence of the movement

00:10:26.889 --> 00:10:31.783
led by Juan Domingo Peron.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:35.160
His trajectory linked
to nationalist sectors

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:35.993
that declared themselves neutral

00:10:35.993 --> 00:10:40.440
during the development
of the Second World War

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:45.440
assisted the figure of General
Peron with European Fascism.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:49.900
Since then a recurring
narrative has been structured

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:52.430
that intends to represent Peronism

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:54.013
as a kind of Creole Nazism.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.830
However, the works of Rannan Rein

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:02.900
have tried to show that the
expansion of citizenship erased

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.840
is (indistinct) by the Peronist Regime

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:06.963
also had positive impact on the Jewish

00:11:06.963 --> 00:11:10.630
who inevitably inhabited the country.

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:13.530
The works show that the
government led by Peron

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:16.360
did not promote any
measures against the Jews,

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.520
and it was even very attentive

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:21.420
to the demands made by the
community leaders in favor of,

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:25.160
for example, facilitating the
entry of Holocaust survivors

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:29.160
or regularizing their citizenship status,

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.220
recognizing the state of Israel

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:32.053
or censoring anti-Sematic
statement published

00:11:32.053 --> 00:11:35.713
by nationalist leaders.

00:11:37.212 --> 00:11:41.950
However, and even for
the spiritual evidence

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:42.783
present by Reins' works

00:11:42.783 --> 00:11:45.807
allowed to corroborate his hypothesis.

00:11:45.807 --> 00:11:46.640
The perspective presented among others,

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:51.640
by Juan Lewis (indistinct)
work on the Peronist right

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:52.836
cannot be neglected .

00:11:52.836 --> 00:11:53.669
That the (indistinct)
character of Peronism

00:11:53.669 --> 00:11:54.502
and it's raw social, programmatic,

00:11:54.502 --> 00:11:55.335
ideological base sheltered
various sectors of Catholic

00:11:55.335 --> 00:12:00.335
and right wing nationalist
that were deeply Anti-Semitic.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:09.480
The period after Peronist
will register an increase

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.340
of escalation of
anti-Semitic speech traits

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:13.403
and practices.

00:12:14.482 --> 00:12:16.860
Leonardo Senkman produced
one of the most prominent

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:20.320
pioneering and systematic
volumes on antisemitism

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:21.430
during this period.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.550
Highlighting some of the central features

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:24.520
during the '90s...

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:26.403
During the '60s and '70s.

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:30.490
First, a continuing
narrative could be identified

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:33.563
upholding the geological
produce of previous decades.

00:12:34.796 --> 00:12:38.182
The Jews were both the
promoters of social revolution

00:12:38.182 --> 00:12:39.900
and financial stipulation.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:44.240
But to which was added the
accusation Double Loyalty.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:48.330
After the creation of the
State of Israel in 1948,

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.140
the nationalist organization
questioned identification,

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.670
solidarity, and financing campaigns

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:55.240
that various Jewish organizations

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:58.150
and prominent personalities developed

00:12:58.150 --> 00:12:59.783
to support the new state.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:04.297
Organizations such as (foreign language)

00:13:04.297 --> 00:13:06.728
and (foreign language)

00:13:06.728 --> 00:13:09.850
were the spearhead of a series
of campaigns that produced

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.087
widespread fear among Jewish organizations

00:13:12.087 --> 00:13:13.673
and political activists.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:18.580
Different attack against
in Edgardo Trilnik in 1960,

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:21.080
Graciela Sirota in 1962,

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:24.770
and the murder of Raul Alterman in 1964

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:27.370
among the most prominent are illustrative

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:30.720
not only of the Anti-Semitic
escalation of those years,

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:31.553
but also

00:13:31.553 --> 00:13:34.360
of the process of radicalization
of political violence

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:37.473
that would characterize
subsequent years in Argentina.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.380
This context must take into account

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:43.970
the reception of the Arab Israeli conflict

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:46.230
that mobilized a broader set of factors

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:48.840
and would give new and changing arguments

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.333
to the discourse against
Jews during the period.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.650
During this first half of the '60s

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:55.903
the accusation of Double Loyalty

00:13:55.903 --> 00:13:58.330
would have the greatest impact.

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:02.170
After the Six-Day War in 1967,

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:03.830
the criticisms would be placed

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:06.730
on the imperialist character
of Israel in the Middle East.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:11.050
This dimension, however, is complex.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:14.440
Not all the actors and
organizations that denounced

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:17.340
the Israeli territorial
expansion in the war context

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:20.120
can be described as Anti-Semitic,

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:23.047
but many others took
advantage of the climate

00:14:23.047 --> 00:14:26.710
of rejection of the world to
legitimize in this public space

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.410
their positioned against the Jews.

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.690
In turn, returning to Senkman work,

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:36.000
one of the most outstanding
aspect of his analysis

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.050
is that he indicates

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:39.710
that the spiral of
anti-Semitic violence did not

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:43.140
necessarily respond to the
characteristic of the political

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.283
and government regimes of the period.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.860
What does mean?

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:50.840
That although there has
been a tendency to think

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:53.290
that dictatorships were fertile ground

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:55.540
for the emergence of the
anti-Semitic narratives

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:56.810
and practice,

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:59.660
the detailed study of the
proliferation of threats

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:00.990
and attacks shows

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:01.990
that their increase was

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:04.640
during the terms of democratic governments

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:09.510
from 1958 to 1966,

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:13.193
and from 1973 to 1976.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:15.170
In particular,

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:18.790
this last period was very
profuse in public demonstration

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:21.413
of rejection of the Jews.

00:15:22.767 --> 00:15:25.480
Dispute within the ruling party

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.100
during the third Peronist period promote

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:29.170
a series of narratives questioning

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:30.580
the representation of Jewish

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:33.550
and their influences in
the search of government,

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:35.180
the business war, the cultural

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.703
and intellectual field,
and political militancy.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:42.520
Following the death of
Juan Domingo Peron in 1974,

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:45.900
for example, his minister
of social welfare,

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.360
Jose Lo Paraja,

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.480
deployed a public and virulent campaign

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:52.740
against the minister of
finances, Jose (indistinct),

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:55.813
which was largely based
on his status as a Jew.

00:15:57.319 --> 00:16:00.120
The presence of Jose (indistinct)
in the ministry of economy

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:03.570
during the administration
of Canberra and Peron

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:05.780
had been the cause of accusations

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:07.860
by the right wing
nationalists organizations

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.020
about the Jewish infiltration in power and

00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:11.063
in Peronism.

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:14.250
In the same context,

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:17.060
two episodes relate to the
conflict in the Middle East

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:18.421
took place with...

00:16:18.421 --> 00:16:20.620
During the Six-Day War.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:21.453
Once again,

00:16:21.453 --> 00:16:23.630
precipitated the question
of Israel and Zionists

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:25.170
in the public debate.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.330
The Yom Kippur War in 1973

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:30.963
and the declaration of the
United Nation organizations

00:16:30.963 --> 00:16:34.773
quoting Zionists as a
kind of racist in 1975.

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:39.100
The reception of both events
serve antagonist sectors

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.650
of the local political
(indistinct) on the right

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:45.130
and on the left to challenge
those who identified themselves

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:47.510
as Jews incorporating into the rhetoric

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:49.380
of the whole Jewish plot,

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:51.920
the accusation about that
colonial dimension of his Israel

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.663
in the context of the Cold War.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:55.820
In this sense

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:57.010
the period characterized

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:59.330
by the radicalization
of political violence

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.130
as its correlate in the produce against

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:04.366
the Jews of many of the
political organizations

00:17:04.366 --> 00:17:09.366
they attacked in those years.

00:17:09.437 --> 00:17:14.437
The military dictatorship
inaugurated on March 24th, 1976

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:18.540
was characterized unlike the
other dictatorial regimes

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.670
that took place in Argentina
during the 20 century

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:23.780
by widely spread repressive policy

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:27.960
whose balance was 30,000
disappeared people,

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.790
500 (indistinct) children

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:33.543
and a significant number of
exiles and political prisoners.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.090
The Never Again report prepared by the

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:40.693
National Commission on the
Disappearance of Person

00:17:40.693 --> 00:17:43.030
(indistinct) and the
report (foreign language)

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:46.660
promote by the democratic
government of Raul Alfonsín

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:49.487
established that the
greatest number of victims

00:17:49.487 --> 00:17:53.050
had concentrated on
certain strata of society.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:56.670
Young people, workers,
professionals, leaders, politicians,

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:58.500
and trade unions.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.990
And that among the universe of affect,

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:02.290
there was in addition

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:05.580
a special treatment on the part
of the perpetrators towards

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:07.873
the individuals who
were identified as Jews.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.570
This representation of Jew
as a special victim of the

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:16.160
last military dictatorship
was forged early

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:21.063
and contemporaneously with the
authoritarian regime in 1976.

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:25.620
On September 28th, 1976,

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:27.010
Bart Levinson,

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:29.580
representative of the
Anti-Defamation League of the

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:32.390
(indistinct) from Latin America

00:18:32.390 --> 00:18:33.610
present his testimony

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:35.660
before a commission of
the chamber of deputies

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:37.280
of the United States of America

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.033
on human rights in Argentina.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:41.330
During his statement,

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:44.030
he point out the large
number of massive publication

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:47.040
that circulate in
Argentina and also allowed

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:50.260
to the fact that several
deaths in terrorist attacks

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:53.553
and of people who have disappeared
were the Jewish descent.

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:57.520
Levinson's pronouncement
started controversy

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:01.150
around a who had legitimacy
to denounce what was happening

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:03.650
and to what extent antisemitism

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:05.350
was a component of the policies

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:07.650
that the dictator regime carried out

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:11.903
in their so-called fight
against subversion.

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:16.260
The first voice that
would be raised against

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:18.970
the representative of the
Anti Defamation League

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.820
would be that of a journalist

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:24.982
who would later recognize himself
as a victim of repression,

00:19:24.982 --> 00:19:26.679
Jacobo Timerman

00:19:26.679 --> 00:19:28.012
However,

00:19:28.012 --> 00:19:29.400
(indistinct) director of L'Opinion

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:32.750
send a letter to North
American Senator Donald Fraser

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:34.630
on October 1, 1967...

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:37.163
'66...

00:19:37.163 --> 00:19:38.040
76,

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:40.640
in his capacity as chairman
of the subcommittee

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:43.730
that deals with the issue of
human rights in my country,

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:46.930
holding a different view of
the declaration of Levinson.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:47.763
Quote,

00:19:48.747 --> 00:19:50.360
"My newspaper, L'Opinion

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:52.850
have dealt with this problem,

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:55.340
human rights at all times.

00:19:55.340 --> 00:20:00.070
Trying to do so objectively
without partiality

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:01.640
concerned about the human rights

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:03.683
of all the countries inhabitants.

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:05.520
In the same spirit,

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:08.120
I feel obligated to point out to you

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:10.860
the danger of hearing partial testimonies,

00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:13.693
which I believe is happening
in that subcommittee.

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:17.200
L'Opinion has condemned all violence

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:19.410
and on several occasions has stressed

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:21.930
that condemning only one of the extremes,

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:24.720
be it terrorists from the
left or from the right,

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:28.003
means being an accomplice
of the other extreme.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:31.300
This leads me, dear Mr. Fraser,

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:34.330
to ask you to be invite to testify before

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:36.770
that subcommission in the conviction

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:38.410
that my testimony will serve

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:39.970
to understand the human rights

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:43.870
of the entire Argentina
population without exclusions,

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:47.420
and to prevent an unnecessary
deterioration of relations

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:49.560
between our two countries."

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:50.393
End of quote.

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:54.720
Timerman request would be paradoxical.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:58.030
He would classify years
later as collaborators

00:20:58.030 --> 00:20:59.470
due to have the same attitude

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:02.220
or refuse to consider the
nature of their arrest

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:04.210
as a part of a anti-Semitic campaign

00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:06.633
by the military dictatorship.

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:09.370
However,

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:13.288
the controversy as a result
of Levinson's statement shows

00:21:13.288 --> 00:21:14.425
that the Jewish question

00:21:14.425 --> 00:21:16.390
was a sensitive vector of
international complaints

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:18.913
about human rights
violations in our country.

00:21:22.585 --> 00:21:24.470
The analysis of documents found

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:29.210
allow us to identify two
distinctive forms of manifestations

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:31.753
of anti-Semitism in the
(indistinct) period.

00:21:32.983 --> 00:21:36.290
One of a public nature and
the other of clandestine.

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:38.321
While the first was characterized

00:21:38.321 --> 00:21:41.110
by the commercial dissemination
of liberal against Jews,

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:43.680
threats and attack against
community institutions,

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:45.640
and even the official attempt to impound

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:48.748
the compulsory teaching
of the Catholic religion

00:21:48.748 --> 00:21:49.583
in public education.

00:21:50.695 --> 00:21:52.706
The second materialized more diffuse.

00:21:52.706 --> 00:21:54.900
The anti-Semitism on the clandestine order

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:57.890
refers to the ways in which
the treatment of the Jews

00:21:57.890 --> 00:22:01.260
was administrated in the
clandestine detention centers

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:03.170
and the various penitentiary units

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.550
where the political
parishioners were houses...

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:09.003
Housed under the exposition of
the national executive power.

00:22:10.370 --> 00:22:13.470
In this sense it could be note
that the public antisemitism

00:22:13.470 --> 00:22:15.330
was one of their central concerns

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:16.580
that continue to mobilize

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.510
the authorities of the
Argentinian Jewish community

00:22:20.510 --> 00:22:23.360
and that obtained positive response

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:25.173
from the dictatorial authorities.

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:27.590
(indistinct) we closed,

00:22:27.590 --> 00:22:28.820
numbers we seized

00:22:29.751 --> 00:22:32.651
and anti-Semitic books from
stores for sale to the public.

00:22:33.827 --> 00:22:36.980
Rabbis were incorporated into
television program enclosures,

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:39.663
the Holocaust series
got broadcast and so on.

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:42.183
However,

00:22:42.183 --> 00:22:43.430
the scope for action around anti-Semitism

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:45.820
of the clandestine in order proved narrow

00:22:45.820 --> 00:22:48.009
and not very permeable for the

00:22:48.009 --> 00:22:50.533
representative of the institutions
of the Jewish community,

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:53.150
The centrally...

00:22:54.254 --> 00:22:56.870
The centrality that the issue
of a special treatment of Jew

00:22:56.870 --> 00:22:59.040
had in the period of democratic recovery

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:01.759
and the debates around the identification

00:23:01.759 --> 00:23:03.610
of the crimes of the
dictatorships with the Holocaust

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:07.646
can be weighed by the effect
they had on actors of national

00:23:07.646 --> 00:23:09.410
and nationalist rights.

00:23:09.410 --> 00:23:13.110
As the work of Jorge Saborido
and Matthias (indistinct)

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:13.960
show,

00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:15.818
the first years of democracy

00:23:15.818 --> 00:23:17.920
replenished in the public space

00:23:17.920 --> 00:23:19.990
the anti-Semitic representations...

00:23:19.990 --> 00:23:22.350
Representations that accused the youth

00:23:23.793 --> 00:23:25.703
of being behind the new government led by

00:23:25.703 --> 00:23:26.683
Raul Alfonsín

00:23:26.683 --> 00:23:28.530
and of the persecution
of those responsible

00:23:28.530 --> 00:23:31.563
for the crimes committed during
the military dictatorship.

00:23:33.020 --> 00:23:36.250
Although the '80s are still
a period of little work,

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:39.300
the aforementioned investigations allow us

00:23:39.300 --> 00:23:41.940
to know the continued nature
of the anti-Semitic discourse

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:43.153
during these years.

00:23:45.372 --> 00:23:47.640
Although there is still no
research to confirm this,

00:23:47.640 --> 00:23:49.890
we could suggest that (indistinct) attacks

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:52.789
on the embassy of Israel in 1992,

00:23:52.789 --> 00:23:56.840
and the (foreign language) in 1994

00:23:57.689 --> 00:23:59.190
anti-Semitism as public rhetoric

00:23:59.190 --> 00:24:01.730
and practice of nationalist Catholic

00:24:01.730 --> 00:24:03.200
and conservative groups,

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:06.130
it maintained a certain
capacity to mobilize sense

00:24:06.130 --> 00:24:08.773
or precipitate polemics in public space.

00:24:09.640 --> 00:24:10.550
However,

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:11.680
after the attacks

00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:14.685
social sensitivity
around the representation

00:24:14.685 --> 00:24:16.435
of the Jew in public space changed.

00:24:19.498 --> 00:24:22.320
This consideration of the
reconfiguration of antisemitism

00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:23.420
after the AMIA bombing

00:24:24.260 --> 00:24:26.859
would not only be a mere
declarative question,

00:24:26.859 --> 00:24:28.295
but the methodological premise

00:24:28.295 --> 00:24:29.980
for those of us who investigated

00:24:29.980 --> 00:24:31.740
the development of
Argentina and Jewish life

00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:33.030
in recent history.

00:24:33.030 --> 00:24:34.690
Why?

00:24:34.690 --> 00:24:37.370
A glance at the contemporary
scene cannot fail

00:24:37.370 --> 00:24:39.480
to notice that the integration of Jewish

00:24:39.480 --> 00:24:42.240
in the various dimensions
that make up the public sphere

00:24:42.240 --> 00:24:44.423
has been in some sense successful.

00:24:45.500 --> 00:24:47.150
Unlike the debates and attacks

00:24:47.150 --> 00:24:49.940
that took place during
much of the 20th century,

00:24:49.940 --> 00:24:51.650
the years we are going through

00:24:51.650 --> 00:24:53.110
show various personalities

00:24:53.110 --> 00:24:55.520
with different degrees
of self-identification

00:24:55.520 --> 00:24:57.220
with the Jewish occupying

00:24:57.220 --> 00:25:01.390
central functions of the
institutional, state, cultural,

00:25:01.390 --> 00:25:03.063
and political fields.

00:25:04.374 --> 00:25:07.274
The same could be said in
relation to the business sphere.

00:25:09.164 --> 00:25:09.997
For some time now,

00:25:09.997 --> 00:25:11.881
the question about the persecution

00:25:11.881 --> 00:25:12.860
or accusations against the Jews

00:25:12.860 --> 00:25:14.133
has been losing weight.

00:25:15.040 --> 00:25:18.050
In any case, controversies emerged

00:25:18.050 --> 00:25:19.710
when the topics put Israel...

00:25:19.710 --> 00:25:22.560
Israel or the Middle East in the center.

00:25:22.560 --> 00:25:23.710
This shift in meaning

00:25:24.742 --> 00:25:25.575
is consistent with the impact

00:25:25.575 --> 00:25:28.119
that the denunciation of anti-Semitism

00:25:28.119 --> 00:25:29.369
has on the public agenda.

00:25:30.460 --> 00:25:33.340
Does this mean that there is
not antisemitism in my country?

00:25:33.340 --> 00:25:35.023
No, not at all,

00:25:36.497 --> 00:25:38.920
but it's evident

00:25:38.920 --> 00:25:41.346
that there is a broad acceptance

00:25:41.346 --> 00:25:43.050
of an integration of
individuals of Jewish origin

00:25:43.050 --> 00:25:45.440
in various (indistinct)
national (indistinct)

00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:47.620
that at times, cast doubt

00:25:47.620 --> 00:25:50.650
on the effectiveness of
their campaigns to denounce

00:25:50.650 --> 00:25:53.100
the persecution and
hatred of Jewish developed

00:25:53.100 --> 00:25:54.650
by local community institutions

00:25:54.650 --> 00:25:56.483
and international organizations.

00:25:57.990 --> 00:26:00.270
Anti-Semitic expressions that
have occurred in the country

00:26:00.270 --> 00:26:02.020
since the beginning of the 20th century

00:26:02.020 --> 00:26:06.282
are more like (indistinct)
versions of the interventions

00:26:06.282 --> 00:26:09.603
and the impact that that those same...

00:26:09.603 --> 00:26:10.610
That those same narratives

00:26:10.610 --> 00:26:12.913
had during much of the 20th century.

00:26:15.314 --> 00:26:18.200
It seems that antisemitism
is less (indistinct)

00:26:18.200 --> 00:26:21.890
to the existence of Jewish
life in the country.

00:26:21.890 --> 00:26:23.660
This could be happening for example,

00:26:23.660 --> 00:26:27.050
in some European countries
where the situation is worrying,

00:26:27.050 --> 00:26:29.456
then the resources for intervention

00:26:29.456 --> 00:26:31.406
and legitimization in the public space.

00:26:32.293 --> 00:26:33.680
National and in the
network of transnational

